{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-183325" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Describe the set $S={5,6,7,...,50}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nS={x\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183325" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The set $S$ contains all natural numbers between $5$ and $50$ (including $5$ and $50$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,5\\le x\\le 50}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\in Z.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,5\\le x\\le 50}.\n$$\n\n- We can write $4<x<51.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,4<x<51},\n$$\n\nor, writing $x\\in Z$ as before, we have\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,4<x<51}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183325" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "590ce8e46628bba34deb00c72f9b8cbcf266ba0c504996d0dd4b26c0ea715221"} {"question" "q-183325" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183325" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "C"] ["math" "N"] ["math" "Q"] ["math" "R"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183325" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "N"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183325" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183325" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183325" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183325" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183325" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "49"] ["math" "50"] ["math" "51"] ["math" "52"] ["math" "53"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183325" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "50"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Describe the set $S={3,5,7,9,11,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n$$\nS={{{field-1}}\\,:\\,n\\,{{field-2}}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n3,\\,5,\\,7,\\,11,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =2 \\\\  & =5-3 \\\\  & =7-5 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in N,n\\ge 1$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =3+(n-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3+2n-2 \\\\  & =2n+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={2n+1\\,:\\,n\\in N}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "590ce8e46628bba34deb00c72f9b8cbcf266ba0c504996d0dd4b26c0ea715221"} {"question" "q-183327" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183327" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2n"] ["math" "2n+1"] ["math" "2n+3"] ["math" "2n-1"] ["math" "n"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183327" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2n+1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183327" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183327" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\in N"] ["math" "\\in R"] ["math" "\\in Z"] ["math" "\\text{is even}"] ["math" "\\text{is odd}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183327" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\in N"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183728" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${1,\\sqrt{2}}$ given below.\n\n${1,\\sqrt{2}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183728" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given set contains the roots $x\\in R$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(x).$\n\nSince the polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=\\sqrt{2},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =3(x-1)(x-\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =3({x}^{2}-(\\sqrt{2}+1)x+\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-3(\\sqrt{2}+1)x+3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{1,\\sqrt{2}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{2}-3(\\sqrt{2}+1)x+3\\sqrt{2}=0}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183728" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "590ce8e46628bba34deb00c72f9b8cbcf266ba0c504996d0dd4b26c0ea715221"} {"question" "q-183728" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183728" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3+3\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183728" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183728" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${-\\sqrt{3},\\sqrt{3}}$ given below.\n\n${-\\sqrt{3},\\sqrt{3}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,2{x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given set contains the roots $x\\in R$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(x).$\n\nSince the polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-\\sqrt{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\sqrt{3},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =2(x-(-\\sqrt{3}))(x-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =2(x+\\sqrt{3})(x-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}-\\sqrt{3}x+\\sqrt{3}x-(\\sqrt{3})^{2}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}+0x-3) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+0x-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{-\\sqrt{3},\\sqrt{3}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,2{x}^{2}+0x-6=0}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "590ce8e46628bba34deb00c72f9b8cbcf266ba0c504996d0dd4b26c0ea715221"} {"question" "q-183729" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183729" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183729" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183729" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Describe the set $S={2,1,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{4},...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n$$\nS={{{field-1}}\\,:\\,n\\in {{field-2}}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051409/state.json" "file_sha256" "e26a8347debe13170f829bfe6cdc9f2f6517a181f5582f1bb3a8b047eb9e0921"} {"question" "q-183792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n2,\\,1,\\,\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{4},\\,…\n$$\n\nform an infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=\\frac{1}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{4}}{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in N,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={4\\cdot {